  "title": "path.join, no .. tricks",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Join names, do not climb out\n\n`path.join(\"logs\", \"today.txt\")` builds a path for *this* folder. `..` is how people try to leave. This lesson refuses it.\n\n`safeJoin(\"logs\", name)` should throw if `name` includes `..`."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "dotdot",
      "promptMd": "`path.join(\"logs\", \"../secret\")` in a careless tool…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "ok",
          "md": "Is always safe",
          "misconceptionId": "path-dotdot-ok"
        },
        {
          "id": "escape",
          "md": "Can point outside `logs`"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "escape"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "safe-join",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> `safeJoin(\"logs\", \"a.txt\")` prints `logs/a.txt` or `logs\\\\a.txt`. Hidden: `..` throws.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "files/main.js",
          "role": "edit"
        },
        {
          "path": "files/hidden.test.js",
          "role": "hidden-test"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "stdout-regex",
          "pattern": "logs[\\\\/]a\\.txt"
        },
        {
          "type": "js-assert"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "if (name.includes(\"..\")) throw new Error(\"no\")"
        },
        {
          "level": 4,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "const path = require(\"path\")\nfunction safeJoin(root, name) {\n  if (name.includes(\"..\")) throw new Error(\"no\")\n  return path.join(root, name)\n}\nconsole.log(safeJoin(\"logs\", \"a.txt\"))\nmodule.exports = { safeJoin }"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": "Join path parts safely. Do not walk above the folder you meant."
}
